        <p>LOCAL NEWS.</p>
        <p>BETHESDA CONGREGATIONAL CHURCH, RUNCORN. There waz a large congregation at Bethesda Congrega- tional Church, Runcorn, on Sunday night, to listen to the secottd of the Rev. J. Simpson's series of sermons on " Modern Prophets and Saints." The preacher took up the life of Mrs. Catherine Booth. Joscrn PRITCHARD, 51, High-street. Runcorn, keeps tin:cram-Es to stilt all sights, from a shilling a pair.—Adat.</p>
        <p>• BURNING FATALITY AT HALE. On Saturday evening a child named Anthony Molloy. two years of age, son of a farm labourer, residing at Hal,;e. wag burned in such a terrible manner about the nVlbat he died the Mewing morning. The child waa tut aiOlse in the house for a short time, and when its Mother returned she found the poor little fellow in flames.</p>
