      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0105" n="art0105">
        <head>COMPANY DRILL PRIZES,</head>
        <p>COMPANY DRILL PRIZES,</p>
        <p>Seven rounds at 200 and 530 yards with drill points added. F. Company—Sergeant J A Rushton, £2. 73; Lance Corporal Gittens. 21 158., 69 ; Colour Sergeant J Mort, £1 10s. 69; Private W H Broady, £1 ss, 62 ; Lance Corporal G Oultram £l, 57; Lance Corporal W Neild, £l5. 55 ; Corporal J. Marsh, 123 65, 54; Private S Joinson,los, 52; Sergeant G R Joynson, Is 65. 52; Pivate E L Platt, Sc, 50. G Comnany—Lance Sergeant W B Cooper, £2, 75; Sergeant D Edwards, Ll 153, 72; eergeant W 1 Haivey, £1 108, 71; Fl ivat e J Houghton, 21 ss, 68; Colour Sergeant J Poole, RI, 66 ; Corporal W H Pheonix, 15s, 54 ; Corporal P Turner, 128 6d, 46 ; Corporal W F Gasket', 10s, 46; Private R Foulkes, Ts 6d, 45; Sergeant T Holmes, 58, 43.</p>
