      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0106" n="art0106">
        <head>RECRUITS COMPETITION.</head>
        <p>RECRUITS COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>Seven rounds at 200 and 3.',0 yards. Private C Garrett, £1,52 ; Bugler.' 1' Edwards, 178 6d, 50; Bugler IV It Joynson, 15s. 46 ; Private James Sadler, 12s 6d. 45 ; Bugler J Mort, its, 38 ; Private WA Marsh, is 6d, 36; Priva' e John Sadler, 5s 33; Private J Coles, ss, 32; Private J T LeCoMeur, 21 6d. 3t ; Private S S Stubbs, 2s 6d, 30; Private W Outhwaite 2s Bd, 30 ; Private G Booth, 2s 6d, 29. EXTRA SERIES.. - _</p>
        <p>Five rounds at ik -t-ants. Sergeant-Instrkctor W Player, silver coffee pot, -.. ; Sergeant W H Harvey, goods, 22; Sergeant J A Rusidon, bed quilt, 22; Private It Shaw, bronze vase. 21 ; Sergeant D Edwards, load coals, 21 ; Corpl. W H Pheonix. pair trousers, 21; Lance-Sergeant W B Cooper, pair trousers, 21; Lance-Corporal 10 Gittens. overcoat. 20 ; Private J Houghton, pair trousers, 20; Private 6 Joinson, bed quilt, 20; Corporal J Marsh, a ham, 20 ; Lance-Corporal W Meld, umbr lia, 20 ; Colour-Sergeant J Mo. t, load pota- toes. 19; Private S Thompson, pair carvers, 19 ' • Bugler J Mort, wool shirt, 19; Bugler J F Edwards. lamp, 18 ; Private C Temple, timepiece. 18; Private Jas Sadler, load potatoes, 18; Lance-Corporal R J Bowen, goods. 18; Private B Hurst felt hat. 18 ; Sergeant T Holmes, goods, 18; Sergesnt J W Woodland, album, 17; Private C Garratt. set vases, 17; Colour-Sergeant 3 Poole. abook, 17 • Sergeant G It joynson, bind quarter mutton, 17; Private J" Walker,hamper potatoes. 17 ; Lance-Corporal G Littlemore, waistcoat, 16 ; Corporal W F Gasket!, 21b. tea, 15 ; Corporal W Walker, goods, 15 ' • Pri- vate J FLeConteur, goods, 15 ; Private C Glover, silk hand- kerchief, 15 ; Corporal F G Coward, goods, 15 ; Private D Wheeler, Ilb tea, 15 ; Lance-Sergeant G Lee, goods, 14. D0N0413 OP stostET PaIXES. Major Hazlehurst, 2:ls. Donors of one guinea :—Captsln D Ashton, Captain G P Ashton, Lieut. Speakman, Mr J Brundrit. S D Chadwick, P Speakman, A Timmins, W Hall- wood, Miss Milner, Canon Heron, Captain Rodger, J B Toft. Donors of 208 Brooke, It N Davies, W Hayes, Dr Robinson, Mrs liazlehurst, A Bulk. Donors of 103 6d : Messrs Wynn Jones, F J Nortnan, T Taylor, 3 W Lightburn, W Mellor, W F Salkeld. J IC Salkeld, G Shone, Q M Berg., Hanklnson. Donors of 10s : -Canon Wood, Dr Carruthers, Dr McLennan, Messrs G L Evans, W Whittaker, W Ii Faro, J Jone 3, H Reynolds, TB Pierpoint, E Imisou, C Dutton, J. Simpson, Isinsker. and Linaker. Mr It Abel 7a 6d. Dooors of sa;—Dr Gastaldi, Messrs 1? A Lake, 11 White. A Salkeld, G Connor, M Barker. J Pritchard, G Moss, T C Price,W Sutton, H Houghton, 3 J W Potter, J Coxbill, J L Jones, C It El Ifarrison. 311 Frith. J Horsefield, W Carroll, J Ditchfield, T , T Sill, W Griffiths. J Savage* G Mason, Jos. Pritchard, Grice. G Is Davies, A Lightburn, 11 Caleburn, A Jordan, 3 H Weston, Crosby and Sons; T C Cooper, Mrs Coward, E Tuckey, Barton, T JODOS, J Meadoweroft. Af Friend 4s. Mr F.Wiswall 4s. A Friend 3s. Mr it Jackson 3s. Ci• Burrows 3s. Donors of 2s 6d each A. Smith, 3 B Holland, T Harris, 14 Marshall, 3 Littler, J E Mt redith. J J Speskman, S C Beckett, J H Harrison, A Woodier, W Nixon, W B Kay, J Dykes. T Grogory, G Horstield, J Johnson, T Bankes, W Owen, J Vose, Mrs Fitton, Mrs Grounds, Mr Rogerson. R Collinge, Exors J Speakman, W Hughes, T H Annett, W ' Cooper, G Percival, Partington and Lancaster, Lowe and Monks, W Garmtt, Aekerley, E Gregory, J Liecester, G Hewett, T Dean, J Dobson, Mrs. Harvey. Mr Picken 2s. Broadhurst 2s. M Nixon 2s. is, each: Mrs Glover. Mrs Roberta, Mnoirs Duckett, Paynter, Green, and H Briscoe. DONORS OF ARTICLES. Mr Fox, felt hat ; Miss Hughes, silk handkerchief; worth Bros. Bros., pair trousers; Mr 11 Morris, umbrella ; Mr Fins- dick, pkg. trousers; Mr J Steele, bed quilt ; Mr S Coventry, pair trousers; Ellwood Smith St, Co. set vases ; Mr Roberts, hind quarter of mutton ;Mr T Haynes, pair Carvers ; Mr Bate, 21bs. tea; Mrs Turner. llb. tea ; Mrs Waterworth, goods ; liandley &amp; Beek, silver coffee pot ;. Lea &amp; Sons, goods ; ?Amin&amp; Son, bed quilt ; Mrs Sherratt, goods ; Mr A; Hough. goods; Mr P Phillips, vest; Mr 3 Sutton, time piece; Mr J Yates. wool shirt ; Mr W Ritderioll, golds ; Mr it Moores.. book ; Dr Preston, bronze vase ; Mr B Kniveton, load coals ; Mr T Yarwood, overcoat; Mr T Griffiths, load potatoes ; Mr T Ford, load potatoes . • Mr J Griffiths, hamper potatoes ; Mr Beech, goods ; Mr J Dutton, lamp; Mr G Bellamy, album; Mr W Collier, ham ; Mr Williams, goods.</p>
        <p>The Celestial Empire is. the only country where no general can ever attain the highest rank. This is con- ceded only to the successful scholar. A traveller visiting Naples recently had his attention called to a placard posted on the door of a little shop in the Via Toledo informing the public that " the title of Duke is offered for sale—inquire within."</p>
        <p>HIGH PRICES FOR CHESHIRE CHEESE.—At the Cheshire dairy farmers' show at Nantwic.h, on Thursday, enorm- ous prices were realised for several prise lots. Two lots made by Mr. J. Dutton, Nantwich , who carried off the silver cup for the best cheese in the yard, realised 1755. and 1725. per cwt. Other pri7.B lotsletcked 11336.4405, and 160 s. per cwt, • -</p>
